%I A398951 #10 Aug 15 2026 07:57:19
%S A398951 29,83,101,191,209,227,299,389,407,443,479,551,587,641,659,677,695,
%T A398951 749,785,803,893,983,1001,1037,1055,1091,1109,1145,1199,1235,1253,
%U A398951 1289,1307,1343,1379,1397,1451,1487,1541,1595,1631,1649,1685,1739,1757,1829,1883,1937,1955,1991
%N A398951 Starts of runs of 8 consecutive odd numbers that are all squarefree.
%C A398951 There are no 9 consecutive odd numbers that are all squarefree, since one number in each such run is divisible by 9 = 3^2. Therefore, these are also runs of exactly 8 consecutive odd numbers that are all squarefree.
%C A398951 The asymptotic density of this sequence is (1/2) * Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 8/p^2) = 0.0246137667188812377382... .
%H A398951 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398951/b398951.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A398951 a(n) == 11 (mod 18) for all n.
%e A398951 29 is a term since {29, 31, 33 = 3*11, 35 = 5*7, 37, 39 = 3*13, 41, 43} is a run of 8 consecutive odd numbers that are all squarefree.
%t A398951 q[k_] := q[k] = SquareFreeQ[k]; Select[Range[11, 1999, 18], And @@ (q /@ (# + Range[0, 14, 2])) &]
%o A398951 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k % 18 != 11, 0, forstep(i = 0, 14, 2, if(!issquarefree(k + i), return(0))); 1);
%Y A398951 Subsequence of A005117, A056911, A069977, and A398950.
%Y A398951 Cf. A007675.
%K A398951 nonn,easy,new
%O A398951 1,1
